Source: fluidmessages-web
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Lin8x <Lin8x@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Lin8x/FluidMessages
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: fluidmessages-web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-aiohttp, python3-tk, openssl, xdg-utils
Recommends: python3-slixmpp
Description: Your phone's texts, calls, and chats on your computer
 FluidMessages Web runs on your computer and shows your Android phone's texts,
 calls, and chats in an app window. Your phone pairs with it over your own
 network, and nothing goes through a cloud service. It can also connect to
 Matrix, XMPP and IRC.
 .
 This package runs from source with the distribution's own Python libraries,
 so OMEMO encryption for XMPP isn't available in it.
